WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.135 --> 00:00:04.105
THE SUMMIT ON TUESDAY, ALSO

00:00:01.937 --> 00:00:05.807
LOOKING BACK AT THIS WEEKEND'S

00:00:04.239 --> 00:00:06.641
G-7 MEETING IN CANADA THAT ENDED

00:00:05.941 --> 00:00:08.944
WITH A BIG BANG.

00:00:06.775 --> 00:00:09.711
WE BEGIN RIGHT NOW WITH CHIEF

00:00:09.077 --> 00:00:10.845
WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT JOHN

00:00:09.844 --> 00:00:13.815
ROBERTS WHO HAS BEEN TRAVELING

00:00:10.979 --> 00:00:14.683
WITH THE PRESIDENT.

00:00:13.949 --> 00:00:16.351
GOOD MORNING, JOHN.

00:00:14.816 --> 00:00:17.419
&gt;&gt; BRET, GOOD MORNING TO YOU.

00:00:16.484 --> 00:00:20.922
WHAT WE'RE WITNESSING UNFOLD

00:00:17.552 --> 00:00:21.289
HERE IN SINGAPORE COULD BE TRULY

00:00:21.056 --> 00:00:22.090
HISTORIC.

00:00:21.423 --> 00:00:23.224
WHAT HAPPENS HERE OVER THE NEXT

00:00:22.223 --> 00:00:25.460
FEW DAYS COULD BEGIN THE PROCESS

00:00:23.358 --> 00:00:28.063
TO ELIMINATE ONE OF THE GRAVEST

00:00:25.593 --> 00:00:32.500
THREATS FACING THE WORLD, OR IT

00:00:28.196 --> 00:00:34.836
COULD GO NOWHERE.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:36.104
PRESIDENT TRUMP TOUCHED DOWN IN

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:38.006
SINGAPORE PRONOUNCING THAT HE IS

00:00:36.237 --> 00:00:39.975
FEELING GOOD ABOUT THE PROSPECTS

00:00:38.139 --> 00:00:42.377
OF HIS MEETING WITH KIM JONG-UN,

00:00:40.108 --> 00:00:43.745
BUT AS HE DEPARTED THE G-7

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.546
SUMMIT IN QUEBEC, PRESIDENT

00:00:43.878 --> 00:00:45.380
TRUMP ACKNOWLEDGED HE WAS FLYING

00:00:44.679 --> 00:00:48.450
INTO THE UNKNOWN.

00:00:45.513 --> 00:00:49.284
&gt;&gt; IT'S UNKNOWN TERRITORY IN THE

00:00:48.583 --> 00:00:51.486
TRUEST SENSE.

00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:55.690
BUT I REALLY FEEL CONFIDENT.

00:00:51.619 --> 00:00:57.158
I FEEL THAT KIM JONG-UN WANTS TO

00:00:55.824 --> 00:00:59.661
DO SOMETHING GREAT FOR HIS

00:00:57.292 --> 00:01:00.095
PEOPLE, AND HE HAS THAT

00:00:59.794 --> 00:01:01.329
OPPORTUNITY.

00:01:00.228 --> 00:01:02.163
AND HE WON'T HAVE THAT

00:01:01.463 --> 00:01:03.331
OPPORTUNITY AGAIN.

00:01:02.297 --> 00:01:03.631
IT'S NEVER GOING TO BE THERE

00:01:03.465 --> 00:01:05.500
AGAIN.

00:01:03.765 --> 00:01:07.702
&gt;&gt; KIM JONG-UN HAD ARRIVED

00:01:05.633 --> 00:01:08.937
EARLIER IN THE DAY TRAVELING

00:01:07.836 --> 00:01:10.972
FARTHER THAN HE EVER HAS AS

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:13.141
NORTH KOREA'S LEADER COURTESY OF

00:01:11.106 --> 00:01:14.542
CHINA'S NATIONAL AIRLINES.

00:01:13.274 --> 00:01:18.246
KIM LATER MEETING WITH THE

00:01:14.676 --> 00:01:18.613
SUMMIT HOST SINGAPORE'S PRIME

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.848
MINISTER.

00:01:18.747 --> 00:01:25.020
PRESIDENT TRUMP WILL MEET WITH

00:01:19.981 --> 00:01:27.989
HIM TODAY.

00:01:25.153 --> 00:01:35.597
THE RED LINE AT TUESDAY'S TALKS

00:01:28.123 --> 00:01:37.899
THE COMPLETE VERIFIABLE

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:39.534
DISMANTINGLING -- DISMANTLING OF

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:41.069
NORTH KOREA'S NUCLEAR PROGRAM.

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:41.703
&gt;&gt; HOW LONG WILL IT TAKE WHETHER

00:01:41.202 --> 00:01:43.304
OR NOT THEY ARE SERIOUS?

00:01:41.836 --> 00:01:43.638
I SAID MAYBE IN THE FIRST

00:01:43.438 --> 00:01:45.140
MINUTE.

00:01:43.772 --> 00:01:46.508
YOU KNOW THE WAY THEY SAY YOU

00:01:45.273 --> 00:01:48.410
KNOW IF YOU ARE GOING TO LIKE

00:01:46.641 --> 00:01:50.345
SOMEBODY IN THE FIRST FIVE

00:01:48.543 --> 00:01:54.482
SECONDS, YOU EVER HEAR THAT ONE?

00:01:50.478 --> 00:01:55.617
WELL, I THINK THAT VERY QUICKLY

00:01:54.616 --> 00:01:57.018
I WILL KNOW WHETHER OR NOT

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.352
SOMETHING GOOD IS GOING TO

00:01:57.152 --> 00:01:59.387
HAPPEN.

00:01:57.485 --> 00:02:00.555
&gt;&gt; BACK HOME, CALLS FOR THE

00:01:59.521 --> 00:02:02.724
PRESIDENT TO BRING WHATEVER DEAL

00:02:00.688 --> 00:02:05.927
HE CUTS WITH KIM TO CONGRESS.

00:02:02.857 --> 00:02:06.995
MASSACHUSETTS SENATOR ED MARKEY

00:02:06.061 --> 00:02:08.997
WHO NEVER ASKED PRESIDENT

00:02:07.128 --> 00:02:09.931
OBAMA'S IRAN DEAL TO BE RATIFIED

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:10.198
SAYS CONGRESS SHOULD HAVE ITS

00:02:10.065 --> 00:02:12.167
SAY.

00:02:10.331 --> 00:02:13.501
&gt;&gt; I THINK IT WOULD BE WISE FOR

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.904
THE PRESIDENT TO COME TO

00:02:13.635 --> 00:02:18.106
CONGRESS TO ENSURE THAT THERE IS

00:02:16.037 --> 00:02:20.809
A RATIFICATION OF ANY AGREEMENT

00:02:18.239 --> 00:02:22.444
WHICH DOES TAKE PLACE BETWEEN

00:02:20.942 --> 00:02:22.777
THE NORTH KOREANS AND THE UNITED

00:02:22.577 --> 00:02:24.279
STATES.

00:02:22.911 --> 00:02:26.381
&gt;&gt; BUT PRESIDENT TRUMP HAD

00:02:24.412 --> 00:02:28.183
ALREADY PREEMPTED MARKEY SAYING

00:02:26.514 --> 00:02:30.018
ON FRIDAY HE WOULD MAKE ANY

00:02:28.316 --> 00:02:31.486
AGREEMENT WITH NORTH KOREA A

00:02:30.151 --> 00:02:33.655
TREATY, UNLIKE THE IRAN DEAL.

00:02:31.619 --> 00:02:34.722
&gt;&gt; I WOULD ONLY DO A DEAL IF I

00:02:33.788 --> 00:02:36.057
GET IT THROUGH CONGRESS.

00:02:34.856 --> 00:02:37.792
I WOULDN'T DO LIKE OBAMA DID.

00:02:36.191 --> 00:02:38.827
&gt;&gt; AS HE ARRIVES IN SINGAPORE

00:02:37.926 --> 00:02:40.562
FOR PERHAPS THE MOST IMPORTANT

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.297
MEETING OF HIS PRESIDENCY,

00:02:40.695 --> 00:02:45.400
PRESIDENT TRUMP LEAVES BEHIND

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:47.368
GRUMBLING ALLIES AT THE G-7,

00:02:45.533 --> 00:02:48.803
AFTER PRESIDENT TRUMP DEPARTED

00:02:47.502 --> 00:02:49.904
QUEBEC, CANADA'S PRIME MINISTER

00:02:48.937 --> 00:02:51.339
RIPPED HIM UP ONE SIDE AND DOWN

00:02:50.038 --> 00:02:53.141
THE OTHER ON TRADE.

00:02:51.473 --> 00:02:55.577
&gt;&gt; IT IS KIND OF INSULTING.

00:02:53.274 --> 00:02:58.813
AND I HIGHLIGHTED THAT IT WAS

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:59.180
NOT HELPING IN OUR RENEGOTIATION

00:02:58.947 --> 00:03:01.282
OF NAFTA.

00:02:59.314 --> 00:03:03.251
&gt;&gt; THAT PROMPTED RETALIATION

00:03:01.416 --> 00:03:04.819
FROM PRESIDENT TRUMP WHO TWEETED

00:03:03.384 --> 00:03:07.088
HE HAS INSTRUCTED OUR U.S. REPS

00:03:04.953 --> 00:03:08.223
NOT TO ENDORSE THE SUMMIT

00:03:07.222 --> 00:03:10.525
COMMUNIQUE AND CRITICIZED

00:03:08.356 --> 00:03:12.927
TRUDEAU AS DISHONEST AND WEAK.

00:03:10.658 --> 00:03:14.562
CHIEF ECONOMIC ADVISOR LARRY

00:03:13.061 --> 00:03:16.064
KUDLOW SAID TRUDEAU STABBED THE

00:03:14.696 --> 00:03:16.598
PRESIDENT IN THE BACK, DOUBLE

00:03:16.197 --> 00:03:18.666
CROSSED HIM.

00:03:16.731 --> 00:03:19.100
&gt;&gt; TRUDEAU DECIDED TO ATTACK THE

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.368
PRESIDENT.

00:03:19.234 --> 00:03:22.170
THAT'S THE KEY POINT.

00:03:20.502 --> 00:03:25.507
AND YES, YOU KNOW, IF YOU ATTACK

00:03:22.303 --> 00:03:26.674
THIS PRESIDENT, HE'S GOING TO

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.443
FIGHT BACK.

00:03:26.808 --> 00:03:31.246
&gt;&gt; KUDLOW ADDED THERE IS NO ROOM

00:03:28.576 --> 00:03:32.247
FOR A SHOW OF WEAKNESS BEFORE

00:03:31.379 --> 00:03:32.614
THIS IMPORTANT SUMMIT ON

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.149
TUESDAY.

00:03:32.747 --> 00:03:35.383
HERE'S THE WAY IT WILL UNFOLD,

00:03:34.282 --> 00:03:36.985
THE PRESIDENT'S FIRST MEETING

00:03:35.517 --> 00:03:38.052
WILL OCCUR AT 9:00 IN THE

00:03:37.118 --> 00:03:40.221
MORNING SINGAPORE TIME.

00:03:38.186 --> 00:03:41.923
IT WILL BE A ONE-ON-ONE WITH KIM

00:03:40.355 --> 00:03:48.396
JONG-UN, JUST THE TWO LEADERS

00:03:42.056 --> 00:03:50.765
PLUS THEIR INTERPRETERS.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:59.174
AN EXPANDED MEETING WILL HAPPEN

00:03:50.899 --> 00:03:58.790
LATER

